                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1774596719560",
                  "code": "RECOMMENDATION_GENERATOR",
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Recommendation Generator",
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "medium"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 5049.297074901863,
                    "y": 10903.572211567705
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1774596770371"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1774596719560_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a contract clause recommendation generator.\n\nYour task is to generate one recommendation for each policy position in the rule JSON.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nINPUT\n\nClause Text:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EVERY_RULES.EXTRACT_CLAUSE_FOR_CURRENT_RULE.$output.result.clause_text}}\n\nPolicy Rule JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EVERY_RULES.$currentItem}}\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n**RULE**\n\n- Use Policy Rule JSON only to understand the target policy positions.\n- Use Clause Text as the source text for recommendation_text when a revised clause must be generated.\n- Use position_text only as the target policy requirement to apply to Clause Text.\n- Do NOT output position_text by itself as recommendation_text.\n- While interpreting meaning, ignore formatting-only noise: newlines, tabs, repeated spaces, special symbols, and numbering artifacts.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n**POLICY STRUCTURE**\n\nPositions may include:\n- standard_position\n- fallback_X_position (X = 1..n)\n\nAssociated fields:\n- standard_clause_number, standard_risk\n- fallback_X_clause_number, fallback_X_risk, fallback_X_approval, fallback_X_approval_authority\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n**INSTRUCTIONS**\n\nFor every supported position defined in the rule JSON, generate one recommendation:\n- standard_position\n- every non-null fallback_X_position\n\nCore recommendation requirement:\n- Treat blank, empty, missing, or null clause_number values as null.\n- If clause_number is null, recommendation_text MUST be a full revised clause text.\n- If standard_clause_number or fallback_X_clause_number exists, recommendation_text MUST be null for that position.\n- Keep the original Clause Text intact except the minimum required edits to fit the target position.\n- Preserve all unaffected sentences, numbering, structure, formatting, and legal wording exactly.\n- Do not output edit instructions, summaries, bullets, explanations, or placeholders.\n- When clause_number is null, recommendation_text MUST be generated from Clause Text by applying the selected position_text edits only.\n\nCRITICAL CONSISTENCY RULE (MANDATORY):\n- If position_text changes a defined term/value, for example duration, number of days, notice period, dates, thresholds, trigger event, party obligation, exception, or condition, update ALL occurrences in Clause Text that refer to the same concept.\n- Do not leave conflicting legacy values anywhere in recommendation_text.\n- If one sentence is replaced by position_text and other sentences still reference old values for that same concept, harmonize those sentences to the new value.\n- \"Minimum required edits\" includes all dependent cross-references needed to make the full clause internally consistent.\n\nFor STANDARD:\n- Use standard_position as position_text.\n- Set approval = null.\n- Set approval_authority = null.\n- Set severity_code = 0_NO_RISK.\n- Set clause_number = standard_clause_number if available, otherwise null.\n- If clause_number exists, set recommendation_text = null.\n- If clause_number is null, generate recommendation_text as full revised clause text aligned to standard_position.\n\nFor each FALLBACK_X:\n- Use fallback_X_position as position_text.\n- Set approval = fallback_X_approval as-is, or null if blank/missing.\n- Set approval_authority = fallback_X_approval_authority as-is, or null if blank/missing.\n- Set severity_code = fallback_X_risk mapped using the severity mapping below.\n- Set clause_number = fallback_X_clause_number if available, otherwise null.\n- If clause_number exists, set recommendation_text = null.\n- If clause_number is null, generate recommendation_text as full revised clause text aligned to that fallback position.\n- Modify only required portions; keep rest unchanged.\n\nUse below mapping for severity_code:\nNo Risk -> 0_NO_RISK\nLow Risk -> 1_LOW_RISK\nMedium Risk -> 2_MEDIUM_RISK\nHigh Risk -> 3_HIGH_RISK\nCRITICAL -> 4_CRITICAL\n\nHTML PRESERVATION RULES (MANDATORY)\n- Clause Text is the source format.\n- If Clause Text contains HTML tags, recommendation_text MUST preserve HTML format.\n- Do NOT convert HTML to plain text.\n- Keep existing HTML structure/tags unchanged except where minimal content edits are required by the selected position.\n- If input has no HTML, output plain text is allowed.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n**OUTPUT**\n\nReturn valid JSON only in this format:\n\n{\n  \"policy_recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"recommendation_type\": \"<STANDARD | FALLBACK_X>\",\n      \"severity_code\": \"<0_NO_RISK | 1_LOW_RISK | 2_MEDIUM_RISK | 3_HIGH_RISK | 4_CRITICAL>\",\n      \"approval\": \"<fallback_X_approval or null>\",\n      \"approval_authority\": \"<fallback_X_approval_authority or null>\",\n      \"clause_number\": \"<standard_clause_number or fallback_X_clause_number or null>\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"<full revised clause text or null>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n**STRICT RULES**\n\n- Output valid JSON only.\n- Do not skip any supported position.\n- Include recommendations for standard_position and every non-null fallback_X_position in the rule JSON.\n- recommendation_type and severity_code must be in SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.\n- Use STANDARD for standard_position.\n- Use FALLBACK_X for fallback_X_position.\n- recommendation_text must be full clause text with just required position changes only when clause_number is null.\n- recommendation_text must be null whenever clause_number exists.\n- Keep non-modified text identical to Clause Text.\n- recommendation_text must be internally consistent with position_text across all related references."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"policy_recommendations\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"policy_recommendations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"recommendation_type\",\n          \"severity_code\",\n          \"approval\",\n          \"approval_authority\",\n          \"clause_number\",\n          \"recommendation_text\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"recommendation_type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(STANDARD|FALLBACK_[0-9]+)$\"\n          },\n          \"severity_code\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(0_NO_RISK|1_LOW_RISK|2_MEDIUM_RISK|3_HIGH_RISK|4_CRITICAL)$\"\n          },\n          \"approval\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"null\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"approval_authority\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"null\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"clause_number\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"null\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"recommendation_text\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"null\"\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1774596770371",
                  "code": "CHECK_MISSING_RECOMMENDATION",
                  "type": "CODE",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Check Missing Recommendation",
                    "sourceCode": "const startedAt = Date.now();\nconst contractId = $context.$variables.contractId || null;\nconst inputRule = $context.$nodes.FOR_EVERY_RULES.$currentItem;\nconst recommendations = $context.$nodes.RECOMMENDATION_GENERATOR.$output.policy_recommendations;\nconst expectedPositions = [];\nif (inputRule.standard_position) expectedPositions.push('STANDARD');\nfor (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {\n  const key = `fallback_${i}_position`;\n  if (inputRule[key]) {\n    expectedPositions.push(`FALLBACK_${i}`);\n  }\n}\n\nconst recommendedPositions = recommendations.map((r) => r.recommendation_type);\nconst missingPositions = expectedPositions.filter((pos) => !recommendedPositions.includes(pos));\nlet res = {};\nif (missingPositions.length > 0) {\n  res = {\n    ok: false,\n    missingPositions,\n    message: `Missing recommendations for positions: ${missingPositions.join(', ')}`\n  };\n} else {\n  res = {\n    ok: true,\n    message: 'All expected positions have recommendations.'\n  };\n}\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  node: 'CHECK_MISSING_RECOMMENDATION',\n  event: 'recommendation_completeness_checked',\n  contractId,\n  rule_code: inputRule?.rule_code || null,\n  counts: {\n    expectedPositions: expectedPositions.length,\n    recommendedPositions: recommendedPositions.length,\n    missingPositions: missingPositions.length\n  },\n  durationMs: Date.now() - startedAt,\n  status: res.ok ? 'ok' : 'warn',\n  error: null\n}));\n\nreturn res;",
                    "returnType": "object"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 5043.297074901863,
                    "y": 11125.572211567705
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1775364345224"
                  },
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1775364345224",
                  "code": "NORMALIZE_RECOMMENDATIONS",
                  "type": "CODE",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Normalize Recommendations",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const recommendations = $context.$nodes.RECOMMENDATION_GENERATOR.$output?.policy_recommendations ?? [];\nconst clauseTextMap = $context.$nodes.AGGREGATE_FETCHED_ARTICLETEXTS.$output?.result ?? {};\nconst inputRule = $context.$nodes.FOR_EVERY_RULES.$currentItem ?? {};\n\nconst normalizeBlank = (value) => {\n  if (value === undefined || value === null) return null;\n  if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() === '') return null;\n  return value;\n};\n\nconst positionTextByType = {};\nconst approvalAuthorityByType = {};\n\nif (typeof inputRule.standard_position === 'string' && inputRule.standard_position.trim() !== '') {\n  positionTextByType.STANDARD = inputRule.standard_position;\n  approvalAuthorityByType.STANDARD = null;\n}\n\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(inputRule)) {\n  if (typeof value !== 'string' || value.trim() === '') continue;\n  const match = key.match(/^fallback_(\\d+)_position$/);\n  if (!match) continue;\n  const recommendationType = `FALLBACK_${match[1]}`;\n  positionTextByType[recommendationType] = value;\n  approvalAuthorityByType[recommendationType] = normalizeBlank(inputRule[`fallback_${match[1]}_approval_authority`]);\n}\n\nfor (const rec of recommendations) {\n  if (rec?.recommendation_type && positionTextByType[rec.recommendation_type]) {\n    rec.position_text = positionTextByType[rec.recommendation_type];\n  }\n\n  if (rec?.recommendation_type && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(approvalAuthorityByType, rec.recommendation_type)) {\n    rec.approval_authority = approvalAuthorityByType[rec.recommendation_type];\n  } else {\n    rec.approval_authority = normalizeBlank(rec?.approval_authority);\n  }\n\n  if (rec?.clause_number && clauseTextMap[rec.clause_number]) {\n    rec.recommendation_text = clauseTextMap[rec.clause_number];\n  }\n}\n\nreturn recommendations;\n"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
